tor index:"],[3259,"**`project_toml` failing** — run `fastskill project init` to create `skill-project.toml`."],[2116,"**`should_trigger` affects pass/fail.** The engine creates an implicit required `skill_invoked` check for each case, with `expected` equal to the CSV value. An explicit `skill_invoked` check that applies to the case replaces the implicit one; `eval validate` rejects a contradictory polarity. Therefore `false` tests non-consultation and `true` tests consultation, subject to the selected backend's observability."],[2089,"**`true`**"],[1197,"**100 skills**: \\~$0.001 (less than 1 cent)"],[2596,"**A new version is written only when a step is accepted**, so version numbers count\n*accepted steps*, not steps. Once any step has been rejected they no longer line up with\nstep indices: if step 0 is rejected and step 1 accepted, step 1's diff is\n`skill_v0000.md → skill_v0001.md`, not `v0001 → v0002`."],[2885,"**Access Control**: Registry access is controlled by authentication"],[1926,"**Add skills**: `fastskill skill add <skill-id>` (registry, Git, or local path)."],[646,"**Advisory judge rows.** A `judge:<name>` row for a judge that does not gate never moves a `check_rate`. It is reported by the `judge_score` metric that names the judge."],[1179,"**API Key Issues**: Check `OPENAI_API_KEY` environment variable"],[2886,"**Audit Trail**: Publishing history is maintained automatically"],[224,"**Authors**: init, validate, eval, and ship skills via the platform."],[2795,"**Automatic rebuilding keeps the index fresh.** After `skill add`, `project install`,\n`skill update`, or `skill remove`, FastSkill\nreindexes automatically (unless `auto_reindex = false` or `--no-reindex`, and only when an\nembedding provider is available), so `resolve` reflects the current skill set."],[227,"**Automation**: `project install --lock` and reproducible installs in CI."],[1196,"**Average skill**: \\~500 tokens"],[1300,"**Behavior**:"],[618,"**Benchmark**"],[2883,"**Blob Storage**: Artifacts are stored securely with checksum verification"],[1966,"**Case-based evals** with `fastskill eval` to test expected behavior against prompts and rubrics"],[1923,"**Cause**: `--yes` was used at a project root without a skills directory.\n**Solution**: add `--skills-dir <path>`, or drop `--yes` to be prompted."],[1922,"**Cause**: a `skill-project.toml` is already present.\n**Solution**: pass `--force` to overwrite it, or remove the file first."],[331,"**Cause**: Another `fastskill` command is currently running and has acquired an exclusive lock on the lock file."],[1925,"**Cause**: the current directory is not writable.\n**Solution**: fix permissions or run in a directory where you have write access."],[343,"**Cause**: The lock file was manually edited incorrectly, interrupted during write, or corrupted by a bug."],[356,"**Cause**: The system cannot determine the standard config directory for your platform."],[1924,"**Cause**: the version (from `--set-version` or `SKILL.md`) is not valid semver.\n**Solution**: use a semver string such as `1.0.0`."],[1920,"**Changing the embedding model invalidates your index.** Vectors from different\nmodels are not comparable — and often not even the same length. After switching\nmodels, run `fastskill index rebuild` before searching, or results will be meaningless."],[2325,"**Check environment readiness**"],[1398,"**Check name**: Ensure the repository name matches what you added."],[364,"**Check permissions**:"],[1869,"**Checks for an existing file**: refuses to overwrite `skill-project.toml` unless `--force` is given."],[2119,"**Checks score the canonical trace, never raw stdout.** Every check below matches against the run's `trace.jsonl` — the parsed, structured event stream. Raw stdout is deliberately excluded: with the `claude` agent it opens with a `system`/`project init` event listing **every skill installed in the environment**, which used to make any skill-name pattern pass vacuously. Assistant text still reaches the trace as message events, so matching on what the agent actually said continues to work."],[2695,"**Checks TOML*&#x2A; — the grading rules that score each response. &#x2A;(Optional, but without it there is no real grading signal — see below.)*"],[2536,"**Checks**"],[2884,"**Checksum Verification**: All downloads include SHA256 checksums"],[2859,"**cksum**: SHA256 checksum of the ZIP artifact"],[2292,"**Claude Code doesn't see a skill:** Confirm it is installed with `fastskill skill list`, and that\nthe skills directory contains a valid `SKILL.md` for it. `fastskill skill read <skill-id>` should\nprint its content."],[222,"**CLI**: single entry point for installs, checks, search, and evals."],[3126,"**Commit `skill-project.toml` and `skills.lock`.**"],[367,"**Commit project lock to git**:"],[1187,"**Content**: Metadata and embeddings used by semantic search"],[1190,"**Content**: Per-skill file hashes used to decide which skills changed since the last run"],[1866,"**Context detection**: `project init` detects whether you're in a skill directory or a project root:"],[2991,"**Converts to internal format** for processing by:"],[363,"**Create the directory manually**:"],[718,"**Creates File**: Writes `skill-project.toml` with basic structure and commented examples"],[2323,"**Cursor doesn't see a skill**"],[1903,"**Custom**: any path you pass via `--skills-dir` or the prompt"],[1902,"**Default**: `.claude/skills`"],[1150,"**Default**: Shows a live progress bar with completion percentage (when stdout is a TTY)"],[2091,"**Defaults verified against source** (`crates/fastskill-core/src/core/manifest.rs::EvalConfigToml`): `timeout_seconds` defaults to **900**, and `fail_on_missing_agent` defaults to **true** — the CLI refuses to run against a missing agent unless you explicitly set it to `false`. Don't assume otherwise from older examples."],[2858,"**deps**: Dependencies (currently empty, reserved for future use)"],[709,"**Detects Context**: Determines if you're in a skill directory (with SKILL.md) or a project directory"],[225,"**Developers**: install, list, read, search for what agents load."],[866,"**Development Mode** (with `skill-project.toml`):"],[357,"**Diagnosis**:"],[2327,"**Direct skill discovery** — Cursor reads installed skills from the skills directory, no sync step"],[368,"**Don't commit global lock**:"],[370,"**Don't manually edit lock files** unless you understand the TOML schema"],[2863,"**download\\_url**: URL to download the ZIP artifact"],[2790,"**Embeddings power ranking when available.** With `OPENAI_API_KEY` set (and\n`[tool.fastskill.embedding]` configured), FastSkill ranks skills semantically using the embedding\nindex."],[2540,"**Epoch**"],[355,"**Error**: `Global config directory unavailable: ...`"],[330,"**Error**: `Lock file is held by another process: /path/to/skills.lock`"],[642,"**Errored trials.** A trial with outcome `error` still carries check results, because the checks ran, over an empty trace. Every negative expectation and every tool-call ceiling passed there vacuously, so folding them would report an outage as perfect restraint. They are dropped from every rate and counted separately."],[644,"**Estimated cost.** Only the vendor-reported figure is summed. When no trial reported one, the line reads \"not reported\" rather than `$0.00`."],[2757,"**Example `checks.toml`:**"],[2729,"**Example `suite.csv`** (has both `train` and `selection` rows, plus a held-out `test` row):"],[1777,"**Example output:**"],[446,"**Example output**:"],[1241,"**Example Output**:"],[1305,"**Example Output**:"],[1373,"**Example Output**:"],[1384,"**Example Output**:"],[2867,"**Example:**"],[1394,"**Example**:"],[3028,"**Example**: If skill-project.toml has `version = \"2.0.0\"` but SKILL.md has `version: \"1.0.0\"`, the marketplace.json will use `\"2.0.0\"`. Similarly, if skill-project.toml has `author = \"New Author\"`, it will override the author from SKILL.md. The `name` field always comes from SKILL.md frontmatter for display purposes, as it is not present in skill-project.toml."],[1330,"**Exit codes**:"],[3119,"**Expose read-only.** For a browsable UI or REST view over your skills, run `fastskill server serve`\n**without** `--enable-write`. Every mutation endpoint returns HTTP 403, so an exposed instance\ncannot install, update, delete, reindex, or refresh anything."],[710,"**Extracts Metadata**: If SKILL.md exists, extracts version, description, and author from YAML frontmatter"],[2860,"**features**: Feature flags (currently empty, reserved for future use)"],[1059,"**File permissions**: Ensure you have read/write permissions for skill directories."],[1189,"**Format**: JSON"],[1185,"**Format**: SQLite database"],[3121,"**Front an exposed port with an authenticating proxy.** `server serve` enforces no authentication of its\nown and is *not* a security boundary. If the port is reachable off your machine, put a reverse\nproxy or sidecar in front that owns authentication, and make sure the app port is not directly\nreachable. Binding a non-loopback address is fine and expected behind such a proxy."],[3144,"**Front it with an authenticating proxy if you expose it.** If the port is reachable on a shared\nor untrusted network, put a reverse proxy or sidecar in front that owns request authentication,\nand ensure the app port is not directly reachable. FastSkill will not police the bind address for\nyou, and binding a non-loopback address is the normal, expected configuration behind such a proxy."],[2464,"**Gate metric options** (per case, then averaged across the split — see\nSetup):"],[2538,"**Gate metric**"],[716,"**Generates Skill ID**: Uses the current directory name as the skill ID"],[3050,"**Git marketplace**: a Git repository with a marketplace document."],[2911,"**Git sources**: `{repository_url}/.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` (via raw content API)"],[2915,"**Git sources**: `{repository_url}/marketplace.json` (via raw content API)"],[1281,"**git-marketplace**: Git repository with